From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dma_pusher: EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT counts where each entry's words
 came from and reports next to JUNK_TRACE

Core patch on mig020-core (the v1.219.020 series, on top of 0232), off unless
EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT is set.

After kraibse's 2c9263140d on Djihads80/Eglantine (cherry-picked there from e17076e388): entries
parsed from anything but their submit copy, by the reason, and how many differ from that copy.

EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT=1 counts every entry. Lines: the first 4 differing entries per reason, "Entry
at ... differs from its words at submit in N words", and every 1,048,576 entries "FETCH_COUNT
differ/compared/seen: ...; lists read again N, dropped words N, new-mark calls so far N". Compared
counts only entries really compared: at =1 an entry on its untouched submit copy is seen, not
compared, and its row says "not compared". =2 also compares those with memory at the parse, which
reads every entry.

DumpCurrentEntry adds those totals and, for the last 64 entries, "FETCH_COUNT -N: entry i at
addr+size words from <reason>, words differing from submit: d, list read again r times, resumed at
word w, k words wanted at its start, GPU-written at fetch a, at this report b". The first nonzero
word the parser drops where a header belongs does the same, at most 4 times and once per entry,
after "FETCH_COUNT dropped word ..." (the first 16): the unknown-method dump comes once a session
and only after the slip, and run 149's kind never reached it.

Reasons the original doesn't have:
- "copy read again after submit": RefreshSnapshot or RefreshDeferredEntries replaced the copy, so
  "submit copy" would be a false label after a suspension. RefreshSnapshot keeps the words as
  submitted in CommandList::first_words, only with the switch on, and every compare uses those: a
  nonzero count on this reason is the refresh itself changing the words.
- "GPU-written page" comes in three: "after a flush", "host copy" and "memory read live". The last
  is a page ReadGpuWrittenCommands calls Synced, read live with no copy behind it.
- "deferred entry" (its slot is unfilled) and "no copy kept" and "empty at submit" (its offset is ~0
  here, the original's read would run off the array on our tree).

Changed from the original: off by default; no cap at 50,000 entries (it counts only entries that
skipped the copy, and no log gives their rate, so whether it would run out before a slip at 10
minutes is a guess; a cap would also end the counting just when it matters); the words compared
are the ones the parser got, so no second read and a host copy of GPU-written words counts; a
resumed entry is compared from its resume word; the last-entries report is new, since the bad
entry is not always the wrong one (run 162: the entries before it left the method open).

EDEN_NX2_PB_CHECK is now read at first use. It was a file-scope static, read before main applies
env.txt, so RecordParsedEntry never kept an entry on the console and "CHANGED since parsed" could
not print. Unset, nothing changes.

The original only looks at entries that skipped the copy, so it can't see an entry left on a stale
copy, and neither can this patch by itself: for that see EDEN_NX2_FETCH_RECHECK's hit lines. With
the switch off the behaviour is T42's; the cost is 32 bytes per queued list and about 3 KiB per
channel. Not built, not run.
